## Finding 1 — the cluster

What most of them look like and sound like, named concretely. "Four of six use a
purple-to-blue gradient and an abstract node diagram" beats "they look similar".

## Finding 2 — the empty position

The claim nobody is making, the proof nobody is showing, the page nobody has. Say
whether it is empty because it is an opening or empty because it does not work, and
why you think so.

## Finding 3 — the comparison the buyer will run

They will open three tabs. On which dimensions does the client lose? Plainly.

## Worth stealing structurally, never visually

A page type that works, an objection handled well, a proof format. Not a look (`§3`).
